course: dictionary
lesson: 724
title: Measuring words with -ful
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A barrowful is a measuring word. It tells you how much, not what a thing is. Look at its parts: barrow is a wheelbarrow, and -ful means full of. So a barrowful is as much as a wheelbarrow can hold.
explain: The Rabbit orders «A barrowful will do, to begin with» and a shower of pebbles rattles in at the window. He wants a whole wheelbarrow-load, not one pebble. Ask yourself: what would fit in that gap? A wheelbarrow full fits, so you have understood it.
explain: Other words ending in -ful work the same way. A spoonful is as much as a spoon holds, and a cupful is as much as a cup holds. Once you spot the pattern, you can work out many new measuring words, even when you have never seen them before.
fact: A barrowful is as much as a wheelbarrow will hold.
fact: «Barrowful» is a noun, and its plural is barrowfuls.
fact: The ending -ful means full of, as in «spoonful» and «cupful».
fact: In Alice in Wonderland, the creatures outside talk of fetching «a barrowful» of something.
fact: Gardeners and farmers often measure soil, muck or stones in barrowfuls.
exercise: «A barrowful will do, to begin with.» What does a barrowful measure? | A tiny spoonful of tea | A small wooden box | *As much as a wheelbarrow will hold | A rabbit's house
exercise: Look at the word spoonful. What does the ending -ful mean? | Empty of | Made of wood | Very quick | *Full of
exercise: Mia says, «We need three barrowfuls of soil for the garden.» Which word tells you the soil is measured? | garden | soil | three | *barrowfuls
test: Ravi says, «Fill a cupful of water for the plant.» What is a cupful? | *As much as a cup holds | A bucket made of tin | As much as a spoon holds | A small bowl
test: Which word is a measuring word made from a thing plus -ful? | *Barrowful | Garden | Rabbit | Pebble
exam: Jayden reads, «The farmer tipped a barrowful of manure onto the field.» What does barrowful mean, and how did the -ful ending help you? | A field full of farmers | *As much as a wheelbarrow will hold, because -ful means full of | A small heap of manure | Two wheels joined by a bar
